/*  The snake game — the vertical slice: model, view and clock each in their own file, and a main
    that wires them.

    ⚠ Not a game yet. Nothing reads a key and nothing decides anything; the body moves because
    the frame number says so. What it proves is the structure — a type crossing three file
    boundaries, a view that takes model values as parameters, a clock the game owns, and a
    blueprint that builds all of them together.

    ★★ THERE IS NOTHING TO PULL. Every name below — `spot`, `at`, `frame-of`, `nap` — is declared
    by another file in `tools/snake/`, and a directory is one namespace. The four `and book`
    wrappers and the pull line that used to sit at the top of this file said, a second time, what
    the folder already said.
*/

For each frame in range 0 to 1, repeat:
    Define body as a series of spot.
    Insert cast at on (4, 8 + frame) into body.
    Insert cast at on (4, 9 + frame) into body.
    Insert cast at on (4, 10 + frame) into body.

    State "frame {frame + 1}:".
    For each line in cast frame-of on (body), repeat:
        State line.
    Done.

    /* The clock earning its place: without this the two frames arrive together. */
    Cast nap on (40).
Done.
